From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:40:15 -0700
Subject: arm64: dts: apple: t6050-j714s-sleep-soc: make the CIO sleep part
 optional

The SoC values file ends with the J714s's USB4 router sleep (acio2, its
DART, the clock protection syscon), which needs nodes only
t6050-max.dtsi has. A board that includes the SoC values without that
router defines T6050_SLEEP_SOC_NO_CIO first. No change for the J714s.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-sleep-soc.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-sleep-soc.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-sleep-soc.dtsi
index 9b0f2f0c337..5ef086dee57 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-sleep-soc.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-sleep-soc.dtsi
@@ -4576,7 +4576,11 @@ &sgx {
  * taking that DART down and back to the live value before using it again. The router's host
  * also needs the port's PHY, which it stops after the router and starts before it. The left
  * port's router was never up in a trace: it has none of this and is powered off for a sleep.
+ *
+ * A board that includes these SoC values without that router (no acio2) defines
+ * T6050_SLEEP_SOC_NO_CIO first.
  */
+#ifndef T6050_SLEEP_SOC_NO_CIO
 &die0 {
 	ps_prot: syscon@2803f0000 {
 		compatible = "apple,t6050-ps-prot", "syscon";
@@ -4595,3 +4599,4 @@ &acio2_dart {
 &apciec2_dart {
 	apple,clock-protection = <&ps_prot 31>;
 };
+#endif /* T6050_SLEEP_SOC_NO_CIO */
